  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(y\\) varies directly as \\(x,\\) and if \\(y=8\\) when \\(x=4,\\) the value of \\(y\\) when \\(x=-8\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-16\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(-2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(4k,\\) \\(k=\\pm1,\\) \\(\\pm2,\\) \\(\\ldots\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(16k,\\) \\(k=\\pm1,\\) \\(\\pm2,\\) \\(\\ldots\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "-16"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Direct variation gives \\(y=kx.\\) From \\(8=4k,\\) \\(k=2.\\) Therefore, when \\(x=-8,\\) \\(y=2(-8)=-16.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Write direct variation as \\(y=kx\\)",
        "Use the first pair to find \\(k\\)"
      ],
